Etherealism isn't a recognized art movement of the Renaissance. Art movements during the Renaissance included, yet not limited to: 

1. Humanism; 
2. Mannerism ;  
3. Tenebrism;
4. Neo-classicism 
However,  Mannerism, which flourished in the 18th and early 20th centuries was most commonly known to birth the ethereal effect within the sublime.
